he should turn to FAR 4, 5, where different uses of so far are considered; the prefixing of in is for the most part not dictated by reasons either of grammar or of sense, so that much of what is there said applies to in so far also:— He did not, with such views, do much to advance his object, save in so far that his gracious ways everywhere
